Package: thunderbolt-tbrxe-dkms
Version: @VERSION@
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms (>= 2.1.0.0), kmod, make, libc6, thunderbolt-tbfix-dkms (= @VERSION@)
Recommends: usb4-rdma-provider (>= 0.2.70), linux-modules-extra-generic-hwe-24.04-edge | linux-modules-extra-generic-hwe-24.04 | linux-modules-extra-generic
Conflicts: thunderbolt-ibverbs-dkms
Replaces: thunderbolt-ibverbs-dkms
Maintainer: AppMana <ops@appmana.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/AppMana/forks-thunderbolt
Description: tbframe + tbrxe Thunderbolt/USB4 RDMA engine (DKMS source)
 DKMS source package for tbframe.ko (session + lossless frame service on
 Thunderbolt XDomain rings) and tbrxe.ko (rxe-derived InfiniBand engine over
 tbframe). Both modules build in one DKMS pass: tbframe links against the
 thunderbolt-tbfix core's Module.symvers and generated header shim, tbrxe
 links against tbframe's Module.symvers, so this package is version-locked to
 the exact thunderbolt-tbfix-dkms release (never mix revisions).
 .
 The modules are NOT autoloaded: no modules-load.d entry is installed.
 Loading is a deliberate act: `modprobe tbrxe` (depmod pulls in tbframe).
 A node runs one RDMA engine at a time; this package conflicts with the
 legacy thunderbolt-ibverbs-dkms, and userspace needs usb4-rdma-provider
 >= 0.2.70 to bind the tbrxe driver id.
